    "did_you_know": "The photographer had been friends with the sitter for over 25 years when she made this portrait.",
    "description": "This environmental portrait shows Noggle’s friend, mentor, and muse, Albuquerque artist Yolanda Shaw Belloli, working almost frantically in her garden in Santa Fe. The two women met when Noggle moved to the city in 1949; they became inseparable friends. When Belloli died in 1983, she left Noggle an inheritance that granted the photographer a new degree of financial security.",
